@startuml run-state
!pragma layout smetana
title M3a admitted run states (no queue)
[*] --> Running : slot reserved / Accepted
Running --> CancelRequested : first UserCancellation / Timeout / Shutdown
Running --> Persisting : persistence wins shared lock
Running --> Faulted : execution failure / no accepted stop
Persisting --> Succeeded : save succeeds and cleanup finishes
Persisting --> Faulted : save or cleanup fails
CancelRequested --> Canceled : work + callbacks ended\nUserCancellation / Shutdown
CancelRequested --> TimedOut : work + callbacks ended\nTimeout
CancelRequested --> Faulted : stop callback or cleanup fails
Succeeded --> [*]
Faulted --> [*]
Canceled --> [*]
TimedOut --> [*]
note right of Persisting
CancelRun returns TooLate.
Timeout cannot replace persistence outcome.
Product Fail can still become Succeeded.
end note
note left of CancelRequested
Slot stays Busy until actual completion.
First accepted reason is preserved.
M2 native calls must return on their own.
end note
note bottom of Faulted
Ordinary run failure leaves the engine Ready.
Stop/cleanup failure faults the engine and blocks admission.
Engine lifetime: Ready -> Stopping -> Disposed.
Ready and IsBusy describe different properties.
end note
@enduml
